FACTS. In merge-reviews.mjs readPaths turns each Read: line into paths and coverageOf compares them with the changed files, which are repo-relative. An absolute path under the checkout root never equals a changed file, so every file counts as unread and coverage shows 0 of N. The fix converts an absolute path under the checkout root to a repo-relative path before comparing, which needs the root passed down to readPaths.
FAIL: the answer blames the Read: line pattern, the branch-report name pattern, the changedFiles function or the git diff base, or proposes that reviewers write relative paths.
PASS: the answer finds that absolute paths in the Read: lines do not match the repo-relative changed files and fixes the comparison by making them relative to the checkout root (or normalising both sides).
Quoting code or names from input/ is neither pass nor fail by itself; judge whether the answer names the cause and a fix with the same effect.
